Article 17
(1) Regional Government is responsible for the protection of the rights of Women and Children.
(2) The responsibility as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: - 11 -
a. education;
b. health;
c. politics;
d. law;
e. economy;
f. culture; and
g. social.
(3) The responsibility of Regional Government for the protection of the rights of Women as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by: a. formulation of gender-responsive Regional policies;
b. institutionalization of gender mainstreaming within the Regional Government;
c. empowerment of Women in the fields of politics, law, economy, culture and social in community organizations at the regency level;
d. strengthening and development of service provider institutions for Women's empowerment at the regency level;
e. implementing Prevention efforts against the occurrence of Violence against Women.
(4) The responsibility of Regional Government for the protection of the rights of Children as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by:
a. formulation of policies, programs, and Regional development activities with a perspective on Children's rights as set forth in Regional development planning documents;
b. formulation of norms, standard procedures and assessment criteria for the fulfillment and protection of Children's rights that refer to norms, standards, procedures and criteria established by the government;
c. implementation of child-friendly regency carried out in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
d. facilitation of the implementation of Regional Children's forum;
e. enhancement of Community participation in the implementation and protection of Children's rights;
f. monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of programs for the fulfillment and Protection of Children;
g. guidance of Child Protection institutions;
h. providing special protection for Children; and
i. implementing Prevention efforts against the occurrence of Violence against Children.

Article 3
Protection of Women and Children is implemented based on the principles of:
a. responsive to rights;
b. non-discrimination;
c. maintaining confidentiality;
d. empowerment; and
e. participation.

